r Education Center Schedule An Appointment Be Curious, Get Experience, Tell Your Story Your liberal arts education provides an essential foundation for any career you pursue.  Critical thinking, writing, the ability to collaborate, and speaking before an audience are all skills that employers highly value.  At the same time, we believe it’s essential for students to have quality, real-world experiences during their time at school through internships, on-campus student employment, and volunteering. At the Boucher Career Education Center we are here to guide your path, providing support to students choosing a major, information on building your résumé and networking, career advice, and much more. Career Education Resources Career Exploration Résumé & Cover Letters Networking & Interviewing Internships & Jobs Career Readiness Micro-Credentials Graduate Study & Service Identity-Based Resources Post-Graduation Success About Us Make an in-person, video, or phone appointment through Handshake . Top floor of the Durick Library – part of the Student Success Center Offices in rooms 302, 304, 306, and 307 Monday-Friday 802.654.2547 careereducation@smcvt.edu . Follow Us: Diversity, equity and inclusion are core values and a priority in all our work. Whether you are a prospective student or family, current student, alumna/us or employer, our career staff is here to help. Check out our strategic plan that guides our work with students, alumni, and employers to build career readiness and a plan for the future. Meet Our Team Career Education Center Ingrid Peterson P'21, P'22 Director, Career Education Center Durick Library, Office 302 - Student Success Center 802.654.2531 ipeterson@smcvt.edu Read more Career Education Center Joe Speidel Career Education Coach Durick Library, Office 304 - Student Success Center 802.654.2470 jspeidel3@smcvt.edu Read more Career Education Center Michael Ewan Career Education Coach Durick Library, Office 306 - Student Success Center 802.654.1909 mewan@smcvt.edu Read more Career Education Center Dina Alsaffar '20 Internship, On-Campus Student Employment, and Peer Tutoring Coordinator Durick Library, Office 307 802.654.2902 dalsaffar@smcvt.edu Read more Destination: Success In the first six months after graduation, 94% of the class of 2022 was employed, continuing education, in an internship, or doing military or volunteer service. St. Mike’s laid a strong foundation for my current higher academic pursuits.  My B.S. in Public Health and Equity Studies gave me invaluable knowledge—from exploring critical public health topics to engaging in independent projects and mentorship roles.  As a leader of the Student Global AIDS Campaign, I was able to apply concepts in class and advocate for change.  With guidance from the career office, I was well-prepared to step into graduate studies and am now pursuing an MPH at Brown University with a focus in global health, continuing to build on the skills and experiences I developed at St. Mike’s. – Greg Hurter ’24 Who is Saint Michael? Contact One Winooski Park\r\nColchester, Vermont, USA 05439 802.654.2000 Resources Canvas mySMC Webmail Catalog Library Academic Calendar Faculty & Staff Resources Graduate Student Resources Institute for the Environment Institute for Global Engagement Prospective Students Request Info Apply Schedule a Visit Financial Aid Majors and Minors Campus Store Contact Admissions Alumni Giving Alumni Events Calendar Reunion Get Involved Contact Advancement About News Events Directory Offices and Services Title IX & Sexual Misconduct Website Privacy Policy Employment Opportunities HEOA Consumer Disclosures Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026  Saint Michael's College Privacy Policy Sitemap"
